# The Pues Manifesto

Nine principles that apply to every Pues project — design, code, docs, and
tooling. They are the shared "why" behind the per-task skills; when a decision
is unclear, these decide it. They are ordered by precedence: when two collide,
the higher one wins. (Several are already used as shorthand in code/docs, e.g.
`STUF`, `POLS`.)

1. **BAIT — Build AI Tools.** Build for agents as first-class users: `--json`,
   stable exit codes, machine-readable contracts, headless paths alongside the
   UI. They are who we serve; everything below is in service of them.
2. **POLS — Principle Of Least Surprise.** Match what people already know (Git
   verbs, platform idioms, existing patterns). No silent magic; behaviour
   should read the way its name promises. Trust is the foundation.
3. **STUF — Show Them Useful Feedback.** Every failure names what happened and
   a literally-runnable way to recover. Errors are actionable, never dead ends.
4. **KISS — Keep It Simple, Stupid.** Prefer the smallest design that works;
   lean on Bun internals and convention over configuration. The simplest thing
   that satisfies the above — not simpler.
5. **DOTE — Do One Thing Excellently.** Each tool, skill, command, and module
   has one clear job done well — not several jobs done adequately.
6. **FIAT — Fit It All Together.** The separate repos compose into one
   coherent whole — loggers drops into any app, Pues vendors its skills/rules
   into consumers — each through a shared contract, not a per-repo reinvention.
7. **WACO — We Are Customer One.** Dogfood everything. If it's awkward for us,
   it ships awkward — fix it where we feel it first.
8. **DAPP — Document All Pain Points.** When something is rough or a tool can't
   do X, that's a finding — capture it (an issue/note), don't route around it
   silently.
9. **FLOW — Feedback Loops On Workflows.** Tighten the find→fix→ship loop; SSE
   keeps every client live, and the workflow should close on itself, not stall.
